          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Saddam Hussein</strong><br>\nSaddam Hussein was born in 1937 in Al-Awja, near Tikrit in Iraq. Growing up in a poor family, his childhood was marked by struggle and the absence of a father figure. He moved to Baghdad to live with his uncle, who was a devout Sunni Muslim and supporter of the pan-Arab Ba'ath Party. This connection profoundly shaped Saddam's political ideology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise to Power</strong><br>\nSaddam Hussein quickly rose through the ranks of the Ba'ath Party, becoming a key member by the 1960s. He played a crucial role in the 1968 coup that brought the party to power in Iraq. By 1979, he became the president of Iraq after forcing his predecessor to resign, establishing a powerful and authoritarian regime.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Leadership and Wars</strong><br>\nAs president, Saddam Hussein's rule was characterized by the ruthless suppression of any perceived opposition. He led Iraq into two major wars: the Iran-Iraq War from 1980 to 1988 and the Gulf War in 1991. These wars had devastating effects on Iraq's economy and its people's livelihoods.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
