          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Human Rights Abuses</strong><br>\nSaddam's government was notorious for its human rights abuses, including torture, mass killings, and the use of chemical weapons against Kurds and other minorities. The suppression of uprisings in the late 1980s and early 1990s led to thousands of deaths and widespread destruction.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Economic and Social Policies</strong><br>\nDespite the conflicts, Saddam implemented several economic and social reforms in Iraq. He nationalized oil resources and used the revenue to build infrastructure, hospitals, and schools. However, his economic policies were also criticized for favoring supporters and creating widespread corruption.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Relations with the West</strong><br>\nInitially, Saddam Hussein maintained cordial relations with the West, receiving support from the U.S. and other countries during the Iran-Iraq War. However, his invasion of Kuwait in 1990 led to international condemnation and the subsequent Gulf War, which greatly strained these relations.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
