          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Gulf War and Sanctions</strong><br>\nThe Gulf War ended with Iraq's defeat and the imposition of severe economic sanctions by the UN. These sanctions were intended to prevent Saddam from pursuing weapons of mass destruction but also caused suffering among the Iraqi population due to shortages of food and medicine.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Saddam's Downfall</strong><br>\nSaddam's refusal to comply with UN resolutions and his alleged possession of weapons of mass destruction led to the Iraq War in 2003. The U.S.-led coalition quickly overthrew his regime, and Saddam went into hiding until his capture later that year.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nAfter being captured by U.S. forces, Saddam Hussein was tried by an Iraqi tribunal for crimes against humanity. He was found guilty and executed in 2006. His death marked the end of a turbulent era in Iraqi history, leaving a legacy of both development and destruction.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
